# .llm-friendly-ignore
# Patterns for files that are exempt from LLM-friendliness checks.
# Each pattern should have a comment explaining why it's exempt.
#
# IMPORTANT: Do NOT add broad ignores like "docs/**" or "src/**".
# These defeat the purpose of the policy. Only add specific,
# justified exemptions below.

# =============================================================================
# Generated files — these are auto-generated, not human-authored
# =============================================================================

# Protocol buffer generated Go code
*.pb.go

# Build artifacts
tovarisch/.zig-cache/
.zig-cache/
build/
dist/
target/

# Vendor dependencies (do not edit these)
vendor/
node_modules/

# Ziggy TypeScript bindings (auto-generated from Zig)
tovarisch/.ziggy/

# =============================================================================
# Binary/cache files that should never be checked
# =============================================================================

# Git objects and metadata
.git/

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store

# Editor swap files
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# =============================================================================
# External data fixtures — only if genuinely too large to decompose
# =============================================================================
# Add specific files here only with explicit justification comments.
# Example:
# path/to/large_fixture.json  # Required for integration tests; too large to inline